From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: studio-vaai <info@studio-vaai.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 11:05:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Name types with Error inside their name by their declared
 Dart name

Only a trailing `Error` is renamed to `Exception` where a type is declared
(`DartCodeOracle::class_name`), but an enum variant's field type and
converter, and the `Optional` and `Sequence` helpers, renamed every `Error`
again. A record such as `InternalServerErrorProblem` was then referenced as an
undeclared `InternalServerExceptionProblem`, and a type registered under both
spellings emitted its `Optional` helper twice. These now use the inner code
type's names unchanged, and the blanket `exception_safe_name` rename is
removed.

Upstream: Uniffi-Dart/uniffi-dart#196 (commit c356e4f), its source change
without the `enum_field_type_names` fixture.
---
 src/gen/compounds.rs | 48 ++++++++++++++------------------------------
 src/gen/enums.rs     |  6 ++++--
 src/gen/oracle.rs    |  5 -----
 src/gen/types.rs     |  5 -----
 4 files changed, 19 insertions(+), 45 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gen/compounds.rs b/src/gen/compounds.rs
